// Logos project — https://github.com/victor-smirnov/logos
//
// wql.peg — the wql! SURFACE grammar for peg_gen_logos, in SCHEMA-EMISSION mode
// (ADR 0012 peg-frontend). It builds the Phase-1 RQuery query-PLAN (the `RQuery`
// schema-enum family, `logos.std.wql.plan`) as first-class Writ schema views —
// `doc.make::<S>()` + typed field writes + `WRef<S>` edges — dogfooding ADR 0011.
//
// PARAMETERIZED surface (the trama! model): the macro is
//   resource <name> = wql!(<real Logos params>){ <query> };
// The PARENS carry a genuine Logos parameter list, re-emitted VERBATIM into the
// generated fn signature. SLICE params (`emps: &[Emp]`) are the query SOURCES —
// a `from`/`join` clause names one by its param name; the row type is the slice
// ELEMENT type from the param list (stamped onto the plan by the HANDLER after
// the parse — the grammar no longer captures `:[Ty]`). SCALAR params (i64 / f64
// / str / bool) are referenced BARE in the EL clause bodies (no `$` sigil; the
// old `with` clause is GONE — the param list is the single type source).
//
// The wql! surface has four shapes; each maps to one RQuery variant. The query
// body starts at `from` — the generated fn NAME comes from the enclosing
// `resource <name> =` binding (delivered as the handler's `name` arg and stamped
// onto the plan node's `fn_name` field after the parse):
//
//   RQSimple — from src var [where P]
//              select [first|distinct] S [order by O [desc]] [limit N|p] [: RTy]
//   RQJoin   — from a x [anti] join b y on ON [where P]
//              select [first|distinct] S [order by O [desc]] [limit N|p] [: RTy]
//   RQAggr   — from a x [where P] group by K
//              aggregate name=fn(arg?),… [having H]
//              select [first|distinct] S [order by O [desc]] [limit N|p] [: RTy]
//   RQFind   — from src var find P              (NO other clause — single-row
//              borrow: the generated fn returns Option<&Ty>, the first matching row)
//
// Pipeline semantics: where → group/aggregate → having → order → project(select)
// → distinct → limit. `having` exists ONLY on the aggregate shape (a predicate
// over the group key + aggregate output names); `order by` takes ONE key
// expression + an optional trailing `desc` (asc default); `limit` takes an
// INTEGER literal or a bare IDENT naming a SCALAR param from the wql!(…) list;
// `distinct` dedups the PROJECTED values; `first` (`select first S`) makes the
// query SINGLE-ROW — the generated fn returns Option<ElemTy> (the first
// projected value in scan order, or in ORDER BY order when `order by` is
// present). `first` excludes `distinct`/`limit` (diagnosed by the walker, not
// the grammar — both parse as independent OPT captures).
//
// ── EMBEDDED-EL CLAUSE BODIES (the ONE cross-grammar coupling) ──────────────
// Every EXPRESSION clause body (where / select / on / group-key / aggregate-arg)
// is EL — parsed by the generated EL parser (el.peg → `parse_expr`), producing an
// `SExpr` root handle wired into the plan node's `WRef<SExpr>` edge. Imported as
// `el`; each `<- el::expr` rule lowers to a cross-grammar embed call: scan the raw
// sub-range up to the next STRUCTURAL STOP and hand it to
// `logos.std.wql.el_parser::parse_expr(sub, doc)` into the SHARED arena.
//
// A WQL clause body does NOT end at a `}}`-style tag close (as Trama's does) — it
// ends at the next structural KEYWORD (where/select/join/anti/group/by/aggregate/
// having/distinct/order/desc/limit/on), a top-level result-type `:` (ternary
// `?:` balanced), or a top-level `,`/`)` (an aggregate arg list). The generator emits a KEYWORD-DELIMITED embed
// close-finder (`embed_find_close`) driven by this grammar's keyword tokens +
// `(`/`[` depth tracking — the schema-mode-gated generalization of the template
// close-finder (logos.peg has no embed, so its output stays byte-identical).
//
// ── SELF-DESCRIBING (Option B) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
// source / var NAMES + the result type + aggregate column names live on the
// plan node as captured-IDENT `str` fields; the walker reads them directly (no
// side tables). Row TYPES are NOT grammar-captured any more — the handler
// stamps them from the param list. Optionality is an explicit `has_*` bool
// flag, derived from "did the OPT capture match" (a `bool` schema field written
// from a `$N` capture emits the presence test `capN != NULLP`).

%meta {
    name:      "wql"
    version:   "1.0"
    namespace: "logos::wql::surface"
    output:    "wql_surface_parser"
    package:   "logos.std.wql.wql_surface_parser"
    prefix:    "Wq"
}

// The wql! entry rule: a whole query → an RQuery root edge handle.
%export { query }

// ── CROSS-GRAMMAR EL EMBEDDING ─────────────────────────────────────────────
%import "logos.std.wql.el_parser" as el

// ── SCHEMA-EMISSION binding ────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The RQuery plan schemas live in `plan`; their `WRef<SExpr>` edge fields
// reference `SExpr` from the `ir` module — so BOTH are imported (one `use` per
// space-separated `use:` entry). `arena: external` → the export takes the
// handler's `&Writ`; `ref_wrap: "WRef"` is plan.logos's edge wrapper.
//
// Fan-out field type (generalizes el.peg's SExprArr `"argfan"`):
//   "fan set_agg  RQAGG_MAX"   spreads a $... array of RQAgg edges into RQAggArr
// The write is `while i<len && i<MAXFN() { node.METHOD(i, rcap.get(i)); i++ }` +
// `node.set_len(i)` — the same shape as `argfan` (= "fan set_arg SEXPRARR_MAX").
//
// A `bool` field written from a `$N` capture emits the OPT-PRESENCE test
// `capN != NULLP` (an OPT capture is NULLP when it did not match) — that is how
// `has_where` / `has_result_ty` / `is_anti` are populated.
// The SELECT-TAIL modifier fields (shared by simple/join/aggregate):
//   sel_first       — `select first …`        (OPT KW_FIRST capture presence;
//                     single-row mode — the fn returns Option<ElemTy>)
//   distinct        — `select distinct …`     (OPT KW_DISTINCT capture presence)
//   has_order/order_key/order_desc — `order by O [desc]` (order_clause? capture:
//                     presence + the key SExpr edge; KW_DESC? capture presence)
//   has_limit       — KW_LIMIT? capture presence (covers BOTH value forms)
//   limit_is_param/limit_param — `IDENT?` (a scalar-param name) presence + name
//   limit_n         — `INTEGER?` capture, token-text decoded to i64 (0 if absent)
%schema {
    use:      "logos.std.wql.plan"
    use:      "logos.std.wql.ir"
    arena:    external
    ref_wrap: "WRef"

    RQSimple { src_name: "str", var_name: "str",
               has_where: "bool", where_pred: "ref SExpr",
               sel_first: "bool", distinct: "bool", select: "ref SExpr",
               has_order: "bool", order_key: "ref SExpr", order_desc: "bool",
               has_limit: "bool", limit_n: "i64",
               limit_is_param: "bool", limit_param: "str",
               has_result_ty: "bool", result_ty: "str" }

    RQJoin   { a_name: "str", x_var: "str",
               is_anti: "bool", b_name: "str", y_var: "str",
               on: "ref SExpr", has_where: "bool", where_pred: "ref SExpr",
               sel_first: "bool", distinct: "bool", select: "ref SExpr",
               has_order: "bool", order_key: "ref SExpr", order_desc: "bool",
               has_limit: "bool", limit_n: "i64",
               limit_is_param: "bool", limit_param: "str",
               has_result_ty: "bool", result_ty: "str" }

    RQAggr   { a_name: "str", x_var: "str",
               has_where: "bool", where_pred: "ref SExpr", key: "ref SExpr",
               aggs: "ref RQAggArr",
               has_having: "bool", having_pred: "ref SExpr",
               sel_first: "bool", distinct: "bool", select: "ref SExpr",
               has_order: "bool", order_key: "ref SExpr", order_desc: "bool",
               has_limit: "bool", limit_n: "i64",
               limit_is_param: "bool", limit_param: "str",
               has_result_ty: "bool", result_ty: "str" }

    RQFind   { src_name: "str", var_name: "str",
               pred: "ref SExpr" }

    RQAgg      { name: "str", fn_name: "str", arg: "ref SExpr", has_arg: "bool" }
    RQAggArr   { aggs: "fan set_agg RQAGG_MAX" }
}

// ── Tokens ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Structural keywords (declared as literal tokens; ordered before IDENT so
// `from`/`where`/… win). Every alpha-keyword literal ALSO drives the embed
// close-finder's structural-stop set (a top-level clause boundary).
%tokens {
    KW_FROM      = "from"
    KW_WHERE     = "where"
    KW_SELECT    = "select"
    KW_ANTI      = "anti"
    KW_JOIN      = "join"
    KW_ON        = "on"
    KW_GROUP     = "group"
    KW_BY        = "by"
    KW_AGGREGATE = "aggregate"
    KW_HAVING    = "having"
    KW_DISTINCT  = "distinct"
    KW_FIRST     = "first"
    KW_FIND      = "find"
    KW_ORDER     = "order"
    KW_DESC      = "desc"
    KW_LIMIT     = "limit"

    // Punctuation.
    COLON    = ":"
    COMMA    = ","
    EQ       = "="
    LPAREN   = "("
    RPAREN   = ")"

    INTEGER = /[0-9]+/
    IDENT = /[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*/

    // Skip whitespace + line comments.
    %skip = /[ \t\r\n]+/
    %skip = /\/\/[^\n]*/
}

// ── Rules ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
%rules {
    // query := the whole wql! block → one RQuery variant.
    // Ordered choice (PEG first-match): the relational shapes are distinguished by
    // a structural keyword after the source; the leading optional `where` can
    // precede `group`, and `join`/`anti` can precede the select. Try join, then
    // aggregate, then the single-row `find`, then the simple scan/filter/project
    // fallback. Each alt re-parses the shared `from src var` prefix (cheap;
    // packrat-memoized).
    query <- join_query
           / aggr_query
           / find_query
           / simple_query

    // ── RQSimple ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //   from src var [where P]
    //   select [first] [distinct] S [order by O [desc]] [limit N|p] [: RTy]
    //   $1=KW_FROM $2=IDENT(src) $3=IDENT(var)
    //   $4=where_opt? $5=KW_SELECT $6=KW_FIRST? $7=KW_DISTINCT? $8=sel_body
    //   $9=order_clause? $10=KW_DESC? $11=KW_LIMIT? $12=IDENT(limit-param)? $13=INTEGER?
    //   $14=result_opt?
    simple_query <- KW_FROM IDENT IDENT
                    where_clause?
                    KW_SELECT KW_FIRST? KW_DISTINCT? sel_body
                    order_clause? KW_DESC?
                    KW_LIMIT? IDENT? INTEGER?
                    result_clause?
                    => { CODE: "RQSimple", src_name: $2,
                         var_name: $3, has_where: $4, where_pred: $4,
                         sel_first: $6, distinct: $7, select: $8,
                         has_order: $9, order_key: $9, order_desc: $10,
                         has_limit: $11, limit_is_param: $12, limit_param: $12,
                         limit_n: $13,
                         has_result_ty: $14, result_ty: $14 }

    // ── RQFind — single-row borrow: `from src var find P` ─────────────────
    // REPLACES where+select: the generated fn returns Option<&Ty> — a borrow of
    // the FIRST row matching P (early-exit scan), None when no row matches. NO
    // other clause may follow (the predicate body ends at EOI; a trailing
    // clause keyword fails the whole-query parse). Ordered BEFORE simple_query.
    //   $1=KW_FROM $2=IDENT(src) $3=IDENT(var) $4=KW_FIND $5=find_body
    find_query <- KW_FROM IDENT IDENT
                  KW_FIND find_body
                  => { CODE: "RQFind", src_name: $2,
                       var_name: $3, pred: $5 }

    // ── RQJoin ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //   from a x [anti] join b y on ON [where P]
    //   select [first] [distinct] S [order by O [desc]] [limit N|p] [: RTy]
    //   $1=KW_FROM $2=IDENT(a) $3=IDENT(x)
    //   $4=anti? $5=KW_JOIN $6=IDENT(b) $7=IDENT(y) $8=KW_ON $9=on_body
    //   $10=where_opt? $11=KW_SELECT $12=KW_FIRST? $13=KW_DISTINCT? $14=sel_body
    //   $15=order_clause? $16=KW_DESC? $17=KW_LIMIT? $18=IDENT(limit-param)? $19=INTEGER?
    //   $20=result_opt?
    join_query <- KW_FROM IDENT IDENT
                  KW_ANTI? KW_JOIN IDENT IDENT
                  KW_ON on_body
                  where_clause?
                  KW_SELECT KW_FIRST? KW_DISTINCT? sel_body
                  order_clause? KW_DESC?
                  KW_LIMIT? IDENT? INTEGER?
                  result_clause?
                  => { CODE: "RQJoin", a_name: $2, x_var: $3,
                       is_anti: $4, b_name: $6, y_var: $7,
                       on: $9, has_where: $10, where_pred: $10,
                       sel_first: $12, distinct: $13, select: $14,
                       has_order: $15, order_key: $15, order_desc: $16,
                       has_limit: $17, limit_is_param: $18, limit_param: $18,
                       limit_n: $19,
                       has_result_ty: $20, result_ty: $20 }

    // ── RQAggr ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //   from a x [where P] group by K aggregate a=fn(e),… [having H]
    //   select [first] [distinct] S [order by O [desc]] [limit N|p] [: RTy]
    //   (`first` PARSES here for a clear diagnostic, but the walker REJECTS it —
    //   group-by emission is multi-row by construction.)
    //   $1=KW_FROM $2=IDENT(a) $3=IDENT(x)
    //   $4=where_opt? $5=KW_GROUP $6=KW_BY $7=key_body
    //   $8=KW_AGGREGATE $9=agg_list $10=having_clause?
    //   $11=KW_SELECT $12=KW_FIRST? $13=KW_DISTINCT? $14=sel_body
    //   $15=order_clause? $16=KW_DESC? $17=KW_LIMIT? $18=IDENT(limit-param)? $19=INTEGER?
    //   $20=result_opt?
    aggr_query <- KW_FROM IDENT IDENT
                  where_clause?
                  KW_GROUP KW_BY key_body
                  KW_AGGREGATE agg_list
                  having_clause?
                  KW_SELECT KW_FIRST? KW_DISTINCT? sel_body
                  order_clause? KW_DESC?
                  KW_LIMIT? IDENT? INTEGER?
                  result_clause?
                  => { CODE: "RQAggr", a_name: $2, x_var: $3,
                       has_where: $4, where_pred: $4,
                       key: $7, aggs: $9,
                       has_having: $10, having_pred: $10,
                       sel_first: $12, distinct: $13, select: $14,
                       has_order: $15, order_key: $15, order_desc: $16,
                       has_limit: $17, limit_is_param: $18, limit_param: $18,
                       limit_n: $19,
                       has_result_ty: $20, result_ty: $20 }

    // ── Shared sub-rules ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // `where P` — the value is the predicate SExpr ($2, past the KW_WHERE token).
    where_clause <- KW_WHERE where_body

    // `having H` — aggregate shape only: a predicate over the group key +
    // aggregate output names. The value is the predicate SExpr ($2).
    having_clause <- KW_HAVING having_body

    // `order by O` — ONE key expression; the trailing `desc` is a separate OPT
    // token capture in the query rule (KW_DESC ends the embedded key body — a
    // structural stop). The value is the key SExpr ($3).
    order_clause <- KW_ORDER KW_BY order_body

    // `: <ResultTy>` — the value is the type-name IDENT ($2).
    result_clause <- COLON IDENT

    // The embedded EL clause bodies. Each `<- el::expr` is a cross-grammar embed:
    // scan the raw sub-range to the next structural stop, sub-parse into `doc`.
    where_body  <- el::expr
    sel_body    <- el::expr
    on_body     <- el::expr
    key_body    <- el::expr
    agg_body    <- el::expr
    having_body <- el::expr
    order_body  <- el::expr
    find_body   <- el::expr

    // aggregate list → RQAggArr fan-out.
    agg_list   <- agg_item ( COMMA agg_item )* => { CODE: "RQAggArr", aggs: $... }

    // One aggregate item: `name = fn(arg?)`. The empty-paren `count()` alt is tried
    // FIRST (PEG ordered choice) so it matches before the arg-bearing form.
    agg_item   <- IDENT EQ IDENT LPAREN RPAREN
                     => { CODE: "RQAgg", name: $1, fn_name: $3, has_arg: false }
                / IDENT EQ IDENT LPAREN agg_body RPAREN
                     => { CODE: "RQAgg", name: $1, fn_name: $3, arg: $5, has_arg: true }
}
